WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
David changes jobs and asks to move retirement money.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.640
First identify the arrangement sending the funds, the arrangement receiving

3
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.100
them and whether the money is pretax, after-tax or Roth.

4
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.580
A properly completed eligible rollover can preserve tax deferral, but a

5
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.620
pretax-to-Roth conversion generally recognizes the previously untaxed amount

6
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:23.080
as income. A receiving employer plan is not required to accept

7
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.020
every rollover. Also confirm whether David is entitled to a distribution

8
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.580
under the sending plan.

9
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.180
Wanting a different investment does not by itself create a withdrawal

10
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:36.440
right. The correct process starts with eligible accounts and an eligible

11
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.340
transaction, before anyone requests a check.

12
00:00:39.877 --> 00:00:44.457
If Rosa moves a traditional individual retirement account directly from one

13
00:00:44.457 --> 00:00:49.177
trustee to another, the trustee-to-trustee transfer is not an owner-received

14
00:00:49.177 --> 00:00:53.827
sixty-day rollover. It is not restricted by the individual-account

15
00:00:53.827 --> 00:00:58.437
one-rollover-per-year rule. For an eligible employer-plan distribution,

16
00:00:59.277 --> 00:01:03.557
a direct rollover sends payment to the receiving retirement arrangement and

17
00:01:03.557 --> 00:01:07.077
avoids mandatory twenty percent withholding on that direct payment.

18
00:01:07.077 --> 00:01:10.337
A check can still qualify as direct when it is payable

19
00:01:10.337 --> 00:01:14.137
to the receiving plan or account for the owner's benefit, even

20
00:01:14.137 --> 00:01:15.597
if the owner forwards the check.

21
00:01:16.357 --> 00:01:19.777
Distinguish who is named as payee from who physically carries the

22
00:01:19.777 --> 00:01:23.337
envelope. Obtain the institutions' instructions and preserve the transaction

23
00:01:23.337 --> 00:01:28.371
records. Suppose an eligible retirement distribution instead is paid to

24
00:01:28.371 --> 00:01:32.971
David personally. A sixty-day rollover generally requires completing the

25
00:01:32.971 --> 00:01:36.731
deposit into an eligible receiving arrangement within sixty days after he

26
00:01:36.731 --> 00:01:39.931
receives it. Intending to roll over the money is not enough,

27
00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:44.091
and depositing it into an ordinary savings account does not complete

28
00:01:44.091 --> 00:01:47.911
a retirement rollover. He may roll over all or an eligible

29
00:01:47.911 --> 00:01:52.571
portion. Any taxable amount not properly rolled over generally remains

30
00:01:52.571 --> 00:01:56.211
income, and an early-distribution additional tax may apply.

31
00:01:57.491 --> 00:02:02.291
Relief from the deadline exists in specified circumstances, but a producer

32
00:02:02.291 --> 00:02:04.251
cannot simply promise an extension.

33
00:02:04.711 --> 00:02:09.731
Confirm the actual receipt date, eligible destination and

34
00:02:09.731 --> 00:02:14.211
applicable exception before treating a late transaction as qualified.

35
00:02:14.991 --> 00:02:20.631
David receives a fifty thousand dollar eligible rollover distribution from

36
00:02:20.631 --> 00:02:24.591
a pretax employer plan, paid to him personally.

37
00:02:25.171 --> 00:02:28.171
Assume the usual twenty percent withholding applies.

38
00:02:29.071 --> 00:02:33.684
Ten thousand dollars goes to withholding and he receives forty thousand

39
00:02:33.684 --> 00:02:38.331
dollars. To roll over the entire fifty thousand dollars within the

40
00:02:38.331 --> 00:02:43.431
ordinary deadline, he must contribute the forty thousand received plus

41
00:02:43.431 --> 00:02:45.211
ten thousand from other funds.

42
00:02:46.371 --> 00:02:50.831
If he rolls over only forty thousand, the unrolled ten thousand

43
00:02:50.831 --> 00:02:53.171
remains taxable under these assumptions.

44
00:02:54.211 --> 00:02:57.291
The withheld amount is a tax payment credited on the return;

45
00:02:57.951 --> 00:03:01.091
it does not automatically satisfy the full rollover.

46
00:03:01.551 --> 00:03:05.851
Also do not treat withholding as the final tax owed.

47
00:03:07.096 --> 00:03:10.896
An owner generally can complete only one covered sixty-day rollover between

48
00:03:10.896 --> 00:03:14.216
individual retirement accounts in a twelve-month period across their

49
00:03:14.216 --> 00:03:18.196
applicable accounts. Opening a second account does not create another

50
00:03:18.196 --> 00:03:22.256
allowance, and January first does not automatically reset the clock.

51
00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.816
This restriction does not apply to direct trustee transfers,

52
00:03:26.296 --> 00:03:30.376
traditional-to-Roth conversions or eligible rollovers between employer plans

53
00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:34.636
and individual accounts. Those transactions still have their own

54
00:03:34.636 --> 00:03:38.756
requirements. The twenty percent withholding example also belongs to a

55
00:03:38.756 --> 00:03:41.136
taxable eligible employer-plan payment.

56
00:03:41.676 --> 00:03:45.656
An ordinary individual retirement account payment to its owner generally has

57
00:03:45.656 --> 00:03:48.536
a ten percent withholding default with election choices.

58
00:03:49.256 --> 00:03:53.056
Do not import one withholding rule into every type of retirement

59
00:03:53.056 --> 00:03:57.657
payment. A required minimum distribution cannot be rolled over.

60
00:03:57.897 --> 00:04:02.137
Employer-plan hardship distributions and other specifically excluded payments

61
00:04:02.137 --> 00:04:06.637
also are not eligible simply because the owner quickly deposits them

62
00:04:06.637 --> 00:04:11.777
elsewhere. Inherited arrangements require additional care: a nonspouse

63
00:04:11.777 --> 00:04:16.497
beneficiary does not have the same owner-style sixty-day rollover choice as

64
00:04:16.497 --> 00:04:19.117
the original owner or an eligible spouse.

65
00:04:20.097 --> 00:04:24.837
A permitted direct transfer must preserve the required inherited-account

66
00:04:25.417 --> 00:04:30.817
identity. Before the transfer is requested, check eligibility, destination,

67
00:04:31.797 --> 00:04:36.417
payment instructions, tax character and deadlines.

68
00:04:36.857 --> 00:04:39.837
A rollover is a tax procedure, not proof that the new

69
00:04:39.837 --> 00:04:41.737
product is suitable or less expensive.

70
00:04:42.417 --> 00:04:48.037
Compare the actual investments, charges, protections
and access rights as a separate decision.
